tgresql-development-cloudbase/references/troubleshooting.md","size":7747,"sha256":"1e061cad4bc9837b670e7eb489feb61f5e79d1895f9dbf381f6d5ef89d4fb8f5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/relational-database-mcp-cloudbase/LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/relational-database-mcp-cloudbase/SKILL.md","size":10702,"sha256":"87e298f3c35c81fd3d1d85b0cfb45958c882d3e7686d5ee0947ec2923c6e5892","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/relational-database-web-cloudbase/LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/relational-database-web-cloudbase/SKILL.md","size":4795,"sha256":"5c5bbcd94eac1b39c2cea37a66182ef554978d71153b70c0f8950f1abb295534","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/scenarios.md","size":1437,"sha256":"c39ee5d1ed08cadc2f0174d2b37a373545001ca63bb3fbe78623e9b8554ca2ac","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/site-onboarding.md","size":10906,"sha256":"b63dfed4ad949606d326f1923ee86ad0d0d90e6d295b80f324ae35a3f123c544","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/spec-workflow/LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/spec-workflow/SKILL.md","size":5152,"sha256":"0ba670e82479068ac9782933c86de42b65fe1608f136e04d0feda5079e018f34","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/tooling-fallback.md","size":8077,"sha256":"e6eb0245394327ce3f8838789fd440dd426d7c483c50fcdff06251f4a5c287a6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/ui-design/LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/ui-design/SKILL.md","size":16009,"sha256":"1e631094677fdd82ed887b4ee6b4c3cd66d98ca21da52ef6bd262ee2c7458d9e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/ui-design/checklist.md","size":838,"sha256":"0ce30d509cde90f2b87ded55b11d87b353a0234f5b513df6ec51d8ce4f7755a0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/web-development/LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/web-development/SKILL.md","size":13846,"sha256":"904673de3a51103297dd8e64acd77b0a4a22e854289c36832b1db3006fb35e1a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/web-development/browser-testing.md","size":5232,"sha256":"9330e4f6c0ee4f5e8eeb06cc2bb86ed144435562823e3a35f78ebcc1a5e8dfaf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/web-development/frameworks.md","size":6201,"sha256":"2e8239bd16e5e0ed5ec22f9ec394cc7919a1cccc3a2d8db7c02454f64a35a4a5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2113,"sha256":"fe4901e731cfd9f8c5427360548436490fe229f3f95ee3a0bbb6b0fdfe1ed8b8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1792380521783,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5fe21ff0010a88672c00f3978f7552354549b2490383313306fb4e00ebd7b7d8","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5fe21ff0010a88672c00f3978f7552354549b2490383313306fb4e00ebd7b7d8","scanners":{"vt":null,"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":277,"checkedAt":1792380521783},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This CloudBase skill is mostly coherent documentation, but it needs Review because it grants broad cloud-management power and includes unsafe guidance around temporary credentials, role permissions, and destructive local cleanup commands.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill instructs use of broad CloudBase MCP/CLI and raw cloud API operations, including examples for destructive environment operations and plaintext temporary credential retrieval. These are coherent for cloud administration but under-scoped for safe default agent use.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is markdown documentation and does not ship executable install scripts, but it recommends user-scope plugin/MCP installation through npx and persistent IDE configuration, which is disclosed and purpose-aligned.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Several referenced agent deployment instructions address the AI directly with MUST EXECUTE language and prescribe raw destructive commands such as deleting ./env as an automatic step. That is over-directive for agent-readable documentation and should be gated by user control.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No backdoor-like persistence was found, but the guidance can persistently change local agent/MCP configuration and can attach cloud IAM policies to service roles, expanding future privilege beyond a single task.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is broad CloudBase development, deployment, debugging, auth, database, AI, and ops work, and the references mostly match that purpose. The capability surface is high-impact because it covers cloud resource creation/deletion, deployment, API calls, user/auth changes, and CAM permission changes.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the agent CloudBase deployment and management authority. Avoid letting it print temporary credentials into chat, confirm any IAM/CAM role-policy changes yourself, and require explicit approval before destructive local cleanup or cloud deletion steps.","findings":"[AE1] expected: The package is a large local reference pack, and the scanner's partial-reference concern is not itself unsafe behavior. The required file and relevant referenced files were available locally and inspected.\n[PE3] expected: Most .env and .env.local mentions are normal cloud app configuration examples or publishable-key storage guidance, not evidence of credential theft. The skill also repeatedly warns against hard-coding long-lived secrets.\n[SQP-2] expected: Temporary cloud credentials are relevant to SDK/API workflows, but the instruction to reveal plaintext STS credentials and feed them directly to SDKs is a material Review concern because it can leak usable cloud credentials into chat or logs.\n[P2] unexpected: The hidden/commented AI MUST EXECUTE directives in the agent deployment reference are over-scoped agent-control language, especially because they sit next to environment-modifying shell commands.\n[TM1] unexpected: Rebuilding a local dependency directory can be legitimate, but the artifact repeatedly presents rm -rf ./env as mandatory and automatic, without sufficient confirmation or path validation.\n[E4] expected: The observability excerpt is trace-context propagation documentation, not conversation exfiltration. Other inspected platform guidance explicitly warns against leaking headers, env vars, and runtime credentials.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1792380521783}}}}}